[[:db/retract 17592186347614 :question/answer-fields 17592186347615] {:db/id "q-161659/real-volume-v1/selection/answer-8sqrt2-3" :answer/id #uuid "72e6b0d3-28f5-5f08-ba4c-ac570bdbafae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161659/real-volume-v1/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "540253a4-0f46-5ab3-a0e1-e391550ba551" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices [17592186347616 17592186347617 17592186347618 17592186347619 17592186347620 "q-161659/real-volume-v1/selection/answer-8sqrt2-3"] :answer-field/correct "q-161659/real-volume-v1/selection/answer-8sqrt2-3" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186347614 :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}},\\,0\\le y\\le 2z}.\n$$\n\nInterpret the unchanged inequalities in real coordinates. The square root requires $2-x^2\\ge0$, so the actual nonempty $x$ projection is $[-\\sqrt2,\\sqrt2]$. Find the volume using this real domain." :question/worked-solution "The inequalities defining $R$ are retained exactly. In real coordinates, $\\sqrt{2-x^2}$ is defined only for $|x|\\le\\sqrt2$. These values also satisfy the printed nominal bound $-2\\le x\\le2$. Thus the actual real solid is equivalently\n\n$$R=\\{(x,y,z):-\\sqrt2\\le x\\le\\sqrt2,\\ 0\\le z\\le\\sqrt{2-x^2},\\ 0\\le y\\le2z\\}.$$\n\nIts volume is\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\nV&=\\int_{-\\sqrt2}^{\\sqrt2}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{2-x^2}}\\int_0^{2z}1\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\\\\\n&=\\int_{-\\sqrt2}^{\\sqrt2}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{2-x^2}}2z\\,dz\\,dx\\\\\n&=\\int_{-\\sqrt2}^{\\sqrt2}(2-x^2)\\,dx\n=\\left[2x-\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_{-\\sqrt2}^{\\sqrt2}\n=\\frac{8\\sqrt2}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe original source accepted $8/3$. That value is the ordinary signed polynomial integral $\\int_{-2}^{2}(2-x^2)\\,dx$. It does not give the volume of this real solid: the source square-root bounds are undefined for $\\sqrt2<|x|\\le2$. All five original choices are retained as alternatives, and $8\\sqrt2/3$ is added as the correct study answer." :question/answer-fields ["q-161659/real-volume-v1/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
